Package: cosmic-pulse
Version: 0.2.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-psutil, python3-yaml
Maintainer: Cosmic Pulse contributors <tramonkamble@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/tramonkamble/cosmic-pulse
Description: Local gaming performance dashboard for Linux
 Cosmic Pulse is a second-monitor performance coach for Linux gaming.
 It samples CPU, GPU, memory, and kernel stall signals at 1 Hz and
 serves a local web UI with Guidance steps and copyable commands.
 .
 Optimized for Pop!_OS / COSMIC; works on other distros with Python 3.11+.
 After install: systemctl --user enable --now cosmic-pulse
 Then open http://localhost:8765